# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks text files out with CRLF, and the generated
# TypeScript contract stopped matching the Rust that generates it — the bytes differed
# even though nothing had changed. Anything compared byte for byte (bindings.ts, GenBank
# round trips, JSON schemas) needs one answer to "what is a newline" on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never translated, never diffed as text. SnapGene .dna files are the reason this
# matters most — DNAgent reproduces a file it only read byte for byte, so a single
# translated 0x0D would corrupt a fixture and break that guarantee invisibly.
*.dna binary
*.png binary
*.mp4 binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.prt binary
*.sqlite binary
*.duckdb binary

# Generated; keep them out of diffs and language statistics.
desktop/src/bindings.ts linguist-generated=true
Cargo.lock linguist-generated=true
desktop/package-lock.json linguist-generated=true
